\begin{align*}
|3+2i| & = \sqrt{3^2 + 2^2} \\
       & = \sqrt{9 + 4} \\
       & = \sqrt{13}
\end{align*}

Now, we multiply these two results together:
\[
|3-2i| \cdot |3+2i| = \sqrt{13} \cdot \sqrt{13} = 13
